prompts.askdata.msg.planner:
{HISTORY}USER QUESTION: {QUESTION}

DATA GATHERED SO FAR:
{GATHERED}

(You have run {COUNT} of max {MAX} queries.)
Decide whether to run one more focused query or to answer now.

prompts.askdata.msg.sql_retry_validator:
YOUR PREVIOUS SQL WAS REJECTED BY THE SAFETY VALIDATOR:
{ERROR}
Rewrite it as a single safe SELECT.

prompts.askdata.msg.sql_retry_exec:
YOUR PREVIOUS SQL FAILED WHEN RUN. Database error:
{ERROR}
Fix the query (check table/column names, joins, types).

prompts.askdata.msg.sql_retry_verifier:
AN INDEPENDENT VERIFIER REVIEWED YOUR PREVIOUS SQL AND REJECTED IT.{PREVIOUS}

WHAT TO FIX:
{FEEDBACK}
Write a DIFFERENT query that addresses this. Do NOT resubmit the same SQL — it would return the same data and be rejected again. If you believe the previous SQL was already correct, make the smallest change that satisfies the feedback.

prompts.askdata.msg.analysis:
{HISTORY}USER QUESTION: {QUESTION}

RETRIEVED DATA:
{DATA}

Analyze this data to answer the question. Show your reasoning and any figures, basing every number strictly on the data above. If a result was capped/partial, compute only what the data supports and say so.

prompts.askdata.msg.synth_no_data:
USER QUESTION: {QUESTION}

No data could be retrieved after retries. Technical detail: {ERROR}

Tell the user honestly (1-2 sentences) that you couldn't retrieve this and suggest rephrasing. Do NOT fabricate an answer.

prompts.agent.supervisor:
You are the supervisor. You coordinate these workers; each one answers its own instruction with its tool:
{WORKERS}
Pick the worker to run next, or FINISH when the results already answer the goal. Do not pick a worker that already succeeded.
Reply with JSON only: {"next": "<worker name> or FINISH", "reason": "<one sentence>"}

prompts.agent.router:
You route the request. {INSTRUCTION}
Pick the ONE branch that fits best:
{CHOICES}
Reply with JSON only: {"branch": <number>, "reason": "<one sentence>"}{NONE_FITS}

prompts.agent.extract_inputs:
Read the user's question and pick out the values of these inputs for one agent run. Today is {TODAY}.
Inputs:
{INPUTS}
Use only what the question states or clearly implies: a relative date such as "yesterday" or "last Monday" becomes a date written YYYY-MM-DD, and a number is written without units or thousands separators. Leave out any input the question does not give; never guess one.
Reply with JSON only: {"values": {"<input name>": "<value>"}, "note": "<one short sentence on anything unclear, or an empty string>"}
